/*
⏱️ Time complexity

O(n²) — every cell is touched once

🧠 Space complexity

O(1) — rotation is done in place
🧠 Simple steps intuition

Flip the matrix vertically (top row ↔ bottom row)

Transpose it (swap matrix[i][j] with matrix[j][i])

After these two steps, the matrix becomes 90° clockwise rotated.
*/
class Solution {
    public void rotate(int[][] matrix) {
        int n = matrix.length;
       //reverse rows of matrix
       for(int i=0;i<n/2;i++){
            int[] temp = matrix[i];
            matrix[i] = matrix[n-1-i];
            matrix[n-1-i] = temp;
       }
       //transpose matrix
       for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
        for(int j=0;j<i;j++){
            int temp = matrix[i][j];
            matrix[i][j] = matrix[j][i];
            matrix[j][i] = temp;
        }
       }
    }
}
